<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rigs up one at 170 in the week.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rigs up one at 170 in the week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 170 rigs under contract in the U.S. Gulf as of May 9, up one from the period ending May 2, Offshore Data Services said Friday.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 180, was 94.4 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in the European/Mediterranean area was down seven at 96 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 105, a utilization rate of 99.1 pct.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count was up two at 576 out of a total fleet of 603, with a utilization rate of 95.5 percent.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
